.TH "PB-TEAM-DEVICE-GRANT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-device-grant - Set all-member or selected-member device capabilities


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team device grant <team> <device-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the complete capability list for one all-member or selected-member grant. Effective access is the union of both grants. Use --active=false to revoke this grant. Team roles alone do not grant device use.

.PP
Set the complete device capability list for one member or all members at the expected team generation. --active can withdraw a grant; omitted capabilities are not implied.

.PP
A personal device can be shared with a team while ownership stays personal, or explicitly transferred to team ownership. Sharing and capability grants are separate decisions. Removing a team-owned device revokes its enrollment; unsharing a personal device withdraws that team's access.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--active\fP[=true]
	set false to revoke this grant

.PP
\fB--all-members\fP[=false]
	grant every current and future accepted team member

.PP
\fB--capability\fP=[]
	exact capabilities: terminal,exec,managed_ssh,files,preview_manage,tunnel_manage

.PP
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for grant

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--member\fP=""
	grant only this accepted member account


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-device(1)\fP
